<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">November 4, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">The live demo sandbox at demo.breederhq.com is now offered across the site as the no-commitment step before the waitlist. It is always the secondary action beside the orange waitlist button, always labeled "Try The Live Demo" with a green live dot, and paired with "No sign-up" where there is room. Links open the sandbox in the same tab.</p>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Placements</h3>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-gray-700 space-y-1">
    <li>Site header (HeaderV3): an outlined demo button left of "Join the waitlist" on wide desktop screens (it is hidden below the xl breakpoint, where the row has no room); an "Explore A Live Sandbox" card above the waitlist card in the Platform menu; and a full-width demo button first in the phone menu's action buttons.</li>
    <li>Homepage hero: "Try The Live Demo" replaces "Browse the Marketplace" as the second hero button (the marketplace stays in the header's Marketplace menu). The assurance row now reads no sign-up / ready in seconds / five years of real-looking records. A bar under the Arcade recording says it is a recording and links to the live sandbox.</li>
    <li>A "Try It Yourself" strip under the Arcade recording on <a href="/heat-cycle-tracking" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/heat-cycle-tracking</a>, <a href="/workflows/heat-tracking" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/heat-tracking</a> and <a href="/workflows/breeding-cycles" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/breeding-cycles</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="/pricing" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/pricing</a> (where /founders also lands): a "Not ready to commit?" note under the Founders' Program application. The form and its submission are unchanged.</li>
    <li><a href="/compare/best-breeding-software" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/compare/best-breeding-software</a>: the "Can I try it first?" answer now says yes for BreederHQ and links to the live demo.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Removed: the private walkthrough</h3>
  <p class="text-gray-700 mb-2">The password-gated "Private Walkthrough" at /demo and /demo/login is deleted; it was no longer used. Both addresses are now temporary (302) redirects in <code>vercel.json</code> to the live demo, so breederhq.com/demo works as a short link to say aloud or share. Both stay out of the sitemap.</p>

  <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-4 mb-2">Tracking</h3>
  <p class="text-gray-700">Every demo link is built by <code>demoUrl()</code> in <code>src/lib/demoLink.ts</code> and carries <code>utm_source=www</code>, <code>utm_campaign=demo</code> and its own <code>utm_medium</code> (header, nav_platform, mobile_menu, hero, hero_recording, feature_heat_cycle_tracking, feature_heat_tracking, feature_breeding_cycles, waitlist, compare_faq, short_link). A click also sends the GA4 event <code>demo_cta_click</code> with the same value as <code>placement</code>, without delaying the navigation.</p>
</article>
